Derived work
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of the design system in packages/ui — the CSS custom-property token
architecture, the motion timing tokens, and the styling of several components
(button, input, textarea, badge, card, checkbox, switch, separator, spinner) —
are derived from the desktop client in the Buzz project.

  Copyright Block, Inc.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  https://github.com/block/buzz

Setu's palette, layout and every other component are its own. The derived
component styles were modified: adapted to Setu's token names, converted to
React 19 conventions (no forwardRef), and documented in place.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Setu's runtime and build dependencies are distributed under permissive licenses
(predominantly MIT, with Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD-3-Clause, MPL-2.0 and 0BSD). No
dependency is under a copyleft license that would extend to Setu's own source.

To re-audit after changing dependencies:

    pnpm licenses list

Two categories are worth re-checking specifically when adding dependencies:

  * MPL-2.0 (currently `lightningcss`, a build-time CSS tool). MPL copyleft is
    per-file and does not reach Setu's sources, but modifications to those files
    would have to be published.
  * Fonts and icon sets, which are redistributed inside the build and usually
    carry an attribution requirement of their own. Add them to the section above.
